// Minimal edit to the LIVE Firestore rules.
// Do NOT replace the live rules file with this snippet.
// Do NOT deploy hosting or functions from it.
// Publish rules only, after editing the live ruleset in place.
//
// Three changes. Leave every other line byte-for-byte the same,
// including hasAdminEmail() (it calls isSignedIn(), so anonymous
// users stay out of admin checks).

// 1. Replace the current isSignedIn().
function isSignedIn() {
  return request.auth != null
    && request.auth.token.firebase.sign_in_provider != 'anonymous';
}

// 2. Add this immediately after isSignedIn().
function isGuestOrSignedIn() {
  return request.auth != null;
}

// 3. In match /botwVotes/{voteId}, change only the create rule's
//    isSignedIn() call to isGuestOrSignedIn().
//
//    Before:
//      allow create: if isSignedIn()
//        && <the existing uid, weekId, band, and time checks>
//
//    After:
//      allow create: if isGuestOrSignedIn()
//        && <those same checks, unchanged>
//
// Every other isSignedIn() use stays isSignedIn().
